{
  "model": "blog.blog",
  "pk": 1,
  "fields": {
    "category": 1,
    "title": "Building My Personal Portfolio Website with Django",
    "slug": "building-my-personal-portfolio-website-with-django",
    "featured_image": "",
    "summary": "In this article, I share the process of designing and developing my personal portfolio website using Django. The project highlights my skills, education, professional experience, portfolio projects, blog, and contact system while demonstrating best practices in web development.",
    "content": "Creating a personal portfolio is one of the best ways for a developer to showcase technical skills and completed projects. I decided to build my portfolio using Django because of its powerful architecture, built-in security, and rapid development capabilities.\r\n\r\nThe project started with designing a clean and responsive homepage that introduces who I am, what I do, and provides easy navigation to different sections of the website.\r\n\r\nTo organize the project, I created separate Django applications for each feature, including:\r\n\r\n• Home\r\n• About\r\n• Skills\r\n• Education\r\n• Experience\r\n• Portfolio\r\n• Contact\r\n• Dashboard\r\n• Blog\r\n• Accounts\r\n\r\nThis modular structure keeps the project organized and makes future maintenance much easier.\r\n\r\nOne of the goals of the project was to create an administration dashboard where I can easily manage my portfolio content without editing the source code. Through the dashboard, I can update my skills, education, projects, blog posts, and personal information.\r\n\r\nAnother important feature is the contact page, which allows potential employers and clients to send messages directly through the website.\r\n\r\nThroughout the development process, I also learned how to:\r\n\r\n• Organize Django applications effectively.\r\n• Build reusable templates with a common base layout.\r\n• Configure media and static files.\r\n• Work with Django forms and model relationships.\r\n• Secure administrative pages with authentication.\r\n• Deploy Django applications successfully.\r\n\r\nBuilding this portfolio has strengthened my understanding of Django development and reinforced the importance of clean project architecture, reusable code, and user-friendly design.\r\n\r\nThis website will continue to grow as I complete more projects, learn new technologies, and share tutorials and development experiences through this blog.\r\n\r\nThank you for visiting my portfolio, and I hope my work demonstrates both my technical skills and my passion for software development.",
    "published": true,
    "created_at": "2026-07-26T12:36:19.391Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-26T12:36:19.391Z"
  }
},
